# Build-context-root ignore file for the 1.f Docker smoke build
# (docs/specs/1f_docker_smoke_build.md, sec 4.3). Works ONLY because the build
# context is architecture/ (sec 4.2): Docker reads .dockerignore from the ROOT of
# the build context, so this is <context>/.dockerignore. A .dockerignore in any
# other subdirectory would be silently ignored.
#
# Load-bearing for the "no secret key material in the image" criterion (sec 7):
# without it honored, `COPY .` would bake the host .secrets/ (CA + node PRIVATE
# keys) and .venv/ into the image. Patterns mirror architecture/.gitignore.
#
# NOTE: this is a SEPARATE file from architecture/.gitignore, which is copied into
# the image and left intact - that one governs the in-container `flwr run` FAB
# build (sec 3.3) and must not be stripped.
#
# Docker .dockerignore does NOT support trailing inline comments (and non-ASCII
# bytes in a pattern crash the BuildKit parser), so keep pattern lines bare.
#
# .venv/       - rebuilt by uv sync; never copy the host venv
# .secrets/    - host CA + node PRIVATE keys; must never enter the image (security)
# .federation/ - run logs + state.db from host runs
# out/         - data + artifacts are mounted, never baked in (Decision 2)
.venv/
.secrets/
.federation/
out/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
